wf-raid-warning = The early warning mast picks up raiders closing in. They land in {$seconds} seconds!
wf-raid-late-warning = Movement on the perimeter. Raiders are almost on top of the outpost!

## Orbital defence

wf-orbital-descent-tracked = The sensor uplink tracks a raid shuttle coming down from orbit. The batteries have it in their sights.
wf-orbital-descent-jammed = The descent jammer scrambles a raid shuttle coming down from orbit. Without an uplink, nothing can fire on it.
wf-orbital-hit = The batteries hit the descending raid shuttle. Its hull is at {$hull}%.
wf-orbital-shot-down = The raid shuttle breaks up in the sky. Its crew won't be landing.
wf-orbital-landing = The raid shuttle makes it through and comes down outside the outpost!

ent-WFOutpostSensorUplinkPack = sensor uplink pack
    .desc = A packed sensor uplink. Use it in hand facing your outpost's floor to set it up there.
ent-WFOutpostSensorUplink = sensor uplink
    .desc = Tracks raid shuttles coming down from orbit while it has power, so the outpost's batteries can fire on them.
ent-WFOutpostFlakBatteryPack = flak battery pack
    .desc = A packed flak battery. Use it in hand facing your outpost's floor to set it up there.
ent-WFOutpostFlakBattery = flak battery
    .desc = Throws flak at raid shuttles coming down on the outpost, while a sensor uplink tracks them. It fires on nothing else.
ent-WFOutpostDefenceBatteryPack = orbital defence battery pack
    .desc = A packed orbital defence battery. Use it in hand facing your outpost's floor to set it up there.
ent-WFOutpostDefenceBattery = orbital defence battery
    .desc = A heavy gun that fires on raid shuttles coming down on the outpost, while a sensor uplink tracks them. It fires on nothing else.
ent-WFOutpostDescentJammerPack = descent jammer pack
    .desc = A packed descent jammer. Use it in hand facing your outpost's floor to set it up there.
ent-WFOutpostDescentJammer = descent jammer
    .desc = Scrambles a raid shuttle's descent while it has power, so it spends longer under the outpost's guns before it lands.

## Who a raid is, as an early warning mast names them

wf-raid-warning-named = The early warning mast picks up { $source } closing in. They land in { $seconds } seconds!
wf-raid-source-camp = a landing party from the Reaver encampment
wf-raid-source-tunnels = tunnel raiders under the ground
wf-raid-source-reavers = an Ashfall Reaver shuttle coming down from orbit
wf-raid-source-drifters = a drifter gang's shuttle
